WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.140 --> 00:00:03.180
- [Narrator] This is the US-made Abrams,

00:00:03.180 --> 00:00:04.020
one of the three types

00:00:04.020 --> 00:00:06.180
of Western style tanks
that Ukraine is expecting

00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:07.410
from its allies.

00:00:07.410 --> 00:00:09.150
And this is the T-72,

00:00:09.150 --> 00:00:11.310
the Soviet era tank that's
been used most frequently

00:00:11.310 --> 00:00:12.900
in the war so far.

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:14.580
As The Wall Street Journal first reported,

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:16.740
the US Senate's allies
have agreed to send tanks

00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:19.650
to Ukraine ahead of more
intense fighting in the spring.

00:00:19.650 --> 00:00:21.900
Abrams and German-made
Leopards are being sent

00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:25.470
to Kyiv in addition to
UK made Challenger 2s.

00:00:25.470 --> 00:00:27.480
So as Ukraine says getting
a significant number

00:00:27.480 --> 00:00:29.670
of those weapons would be a game changer,

00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:31.860
here's how heavy vehicles
from the West match up

00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:35.016
to Russia's older, but
much larger tank fleet.

00:00:35.016 --> 00:00:36.810
(weapon firing)

00:00:36.810 --> 00:00:38.880
First, let's look at why Ukraine argues

00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:40.560
that tanks are so important.

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:41.700
- So the front lines

00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:44.280
of this war have been pretty
static in the last few months.

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:46.380
A lot of the fighting
has been taking place

00:00:46.380 --> 00:00:49.800
along these vast plains
and on small hills,

00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:50.970
and that's the kind of terrain

00:00:50.970 --> 00:00:53.430
and landscape that allows
the big military vehicles

00:00:53.430 --> 00:00:55.143
to operate pretty efficiently.

00:00:56.670 --> 00:00:57.540
- [Narrator] The two main types

00:00:57.540 --> 00:00:58.830
of armored vehicles being used

00:00:58.830 --> 00:01:01.200
in Ukraine right now are main battle tanks

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:04.770
and infantry fighting
vehicles, also known as IFVs,

00:01:04.770 --> 00:01:08.400
tanks of heavy armor, big
guns and caterpillar treads.

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:10.350
When tanks face each
other on the battlefield,

00:01:10.350 --> 00:01:12.120
military experts say they typically look

00:01:12.120 --> 00:01:14.580
for a weak point along
the front line to try

00:01:14.580 --> 00:01:17.160
and break through and
destroy other heavy vehicles.

00:01:17.160 --> 00:01:19.800
IFVs, on the other hand,
are smaller and lighter.

00:01:19.800 --> 00:01:21.960
They have some of the
characteristics of tanks

00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:24.450
but their main purpose is
transporting infantry safely

00:01:24.450 --> 00:01:27.210
around the battlefield while
also providing fire support

00:01:27.210 --> 00:01:28.920
with their smaller weapons.

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:31.350
Prior to the invasion,
Ukraine had significantly

00:01:31.350 --> 00:01:33.570
fewer armored fighting
vehicles than Russia.

00:01:33.570 --> 00:01:35.580
- But now Kyiv's NATO allies

00:01:35.580 --> 00:01:38.640
are sending more modern
military vehicles to Ukraine.

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:40.038
- Today I'm announcing

00:01:40.038 --> 00:01:43.380
that the United States will
be sending 31 Abram tanks

00:01:43.380 --> 00:01:47.790
to Ukraine, the equivalent
of one Ukrainian battalion.

00:01:47.790 --> 00:01:48.990
- [Narrator] So how will Western Tanks

00:01:48.990 --> 00:01:50.850
help Ukrainian forces?

00:01:50.850 --> 00:01:51.900
- Well, for tanks,

00:01:51.900 --> 00:01:54.453
the most important
factor is survivability.

00:01:55.470 --> 00:01:57.390
- [Narrator] Weapons experts
measure this by estimating

00:01:57.390 --> 00:02:00.210
how resistant the vehicles
are to anti-tank weapons,

00:02:00.210 --> 00:02:02.589
like the US-made Javelin
or the Russian Kornet,

00:02:02.589 --> 00:02:06.390
as well as armor-piecing
rounds fired by other tanks.

00:02:06.390 --> 00:02:09.150
Analysts say the Challenger
2 and Abrams tanks,

00:02:09.150 --> 00:02:11.130
which were both used in the Iraq war,

00:02:11.130 --> 00:02:13.860
are some of the most
protected tanks in the world.

00:02:13.860 --> 00:02:15.660
That's because they both
have a composite armor

00:02:15.660 --> 00:02:16.890
called Chobham.

00:02:16.890 --> 00:02:19.080
It uses a combination of steel, ceramics

00:02:19.080 --> 00:02:22.620
and other materials to create
particularly resistant plates.

00:02:22.620 --> 00:02:24.960
Military analysts say
this protection gives them

00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:27.153
a major advantage over the T-72,

00:02:27.153 --> 00:02:29.370
over 500 of which have
been destroyed so far

00:02:29.370 --> 00:02:31.050
in the Ukraine war.

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:32.070
German-made Leopard tanks

00:02:32.070 --> 00:02:34.320
don't use that same armor technology

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:35.850
but have other similar characteristics

00:02:35.850 --> 00:02:38.010
to the Abrams and Challenger 2,

00:02:38.010 --> 00:02:40.380
all three types of
advanced computer systems

00:02:40.380 --> 00:02:42.870
and modern 120 millimeter guns.

00:02:42.870 --> 00:02:44.850
Military analysts say
they're less vulnerable

00:02:44.850 --> 00:02:47.640
than the gun on the T-72,
which hold this ammunition

00:02:47.640 --> 00:02:49.040
at the bottom of the turret.

00:02:50.100 --> 00:02:52.440
On the ground, the tanks,
which are expensive,

00:02:52.440 --> 00:02:55.320
and fewer number will also
get some extra support.

00:02:55.320 --> 00:02:58.050
- Other armored vehicles
are just as important

00:02:58.050 --> 00:02:59.490
and the US has also promised

00:02:59.490 --> 00:03:03.900
to deliver 50 M2 Bradley
fighting vehicles to Ukraine.

00:03:03.900 --> 00:03:04.800
- The Bradley has a number

00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:07.440
of modern advantages,
including thermal imaging

00:03:07.440 --> 00:03:09.690
quicker reload times, and
an armor that's believed

00:03:09.690 --> 00:03:12.360
to be more resistant than
the Russian equivalents.

00:03:12.360 --> 00:03:14.610
That includes the Soviet era BMP-2,

00:03:14.610 --> 00:03:17.310
which have been commonly
used in the war so far.

00:03:17.310 --> 00:03:18.990
Hundreds of these vehicles
have been destroyed

00:03:18.990 --> 00:03:22.020
in Ukraine according to the
military tracking site Oryx,

00:03:22.020 --> 00:03:24.540
while the US says only
three Bradleys were lost

00:03:24.540 --> 00:03:25.533
in the Iraq war.

00:03:27.435 --> 00:03:29.400
(soldiers speaking in foreign language)

00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:31.800
But once Ukraine's forces get new tanks,

00:03:31.800 --> 00:03:34.050
using them effectively won't be easy.

00:03:34.050 --> 00:03:36.210
Many of these systems
use different ammunition

00:03:36.210 --> 00:03:38.430
and require their own
maintenance schedules.

00:03:38.430 --> 00:03:40.140
- It's still going to take a few months

00:03:40.140 --> 00:03:43.110
to set up the supply
chains, the fuel lines

00:03:43.110 --> 00:03:45.000
and the trained crews needed

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:47.670
for the Ukraine to take
advantage of these weapons.

00:03:47.670 --> 00:03:49.920
And the few amounts that
have been promised so far

00:03:49.920 --> 00:03:50.970
make it unlikely

00:03:50.970 --> 00:03:53.940
that it's going to impact
the war anytime soon.

00:03:53.940 --> 00:03:54.840
- [Narrator] Battlefield conditions

00:03:54.840 --> 00:03:56.640
could also reduce their effectiveness.

00:03:56.640 --> 00:03:58.110
The Western systems are heavier,

00:03:58.110 --> 00:03:59.550
meaning that they can be more limited

00:03:59.550 --> 00:04:01.863
when in boggy areas and crossing bridges.

00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:05.100
Although its fleet is
aging and diminished,

00:04:05.100 --> 00:04:07.623
Moscow has hundreds more
tanks in storage centers.

00:04:08.610 --> 00:04:10.950
Ukraine, on the other hand,
says it needs 300 tanks

00:04:10.950 --> 00:04:13.376
to push back Russian forces, many more

00:04:13.376 --> 00:04:16.023
than the initial shipments
expected from the West.

